WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.974 --> 00:00:07.079
Welcome to Home Comfort NY, a study by SUNY ESF, in Syracuse, New York.

2
00:00:07.079 --> 00:00:10.889
This video shows you, step by step, how to take part:

3
00:00:10.889 --> 00:00:14.987
from the study page, to joining, to your daily check-ins.

4
00:00:16.083 --> 00:00:20.926
Start by opening the study link in Safari on your iPhone, and read the study page.

5
00:00:21.316 --> 00:00:23.210
Taking part means three things.

6
00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:28.341
Once, you answer some questions about yourself and your home, which takes about five

7
00:00:28.341 --> 00:00:28.829
minutes.

8
00:00:28.829 --> 00:00:33.899
Then, for one month, from October 20 to November 20, you check in a few times a day

9
00:00:33.899 --> 00:00:35.182
while you're at home.

10
00:00:35.182 --> 00:00:40.068
And you keep one or two small sensors in your home, which you return at the end.

11
00:00:40.463 --> 00:00:43.268
Each check-in starts with one simple question:

12
00:00:43.268 --> 00:00:44.853
how do you feel right now?

13
00:00:44.853 --> 00:00:46.987
From cold, through neutral, to hot.

14
00:00:46.987 --> 00:00:48.634
There are no wrong answers.

15
00:00:49.029 --> 00:00:54.637
Adults living anywhere in New York State can take part, in any kind of home:

16
00:00:54.637 --> 00:00:56.777
owned, rented, or subsidized.

17
00:00:56.777 --> 00:00:59.286
You'll need an iPhone with iOS 16.

18
00:00:59.286 --> 00:01:02.533
4 or later, or an Android phone with Chrome.

19
00:01:02.922 --> 00:01:08.093
Your check-ins are filed under a study code, never under your name, and only the

20
00:01:08.093 --> 00:01:09.450
study team sees them.

21
00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:11.583
The app never uses your location.

22
00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:15.080
Further down are answers to common questions.

23
00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:20.675
Your main contact is Alireza Khodayarkhani, and the email address is on the page.

24
00:01:21.059 --> 00:01:22.389
When you're ready, tap:

25
00:01:22.389 --> 00:01:23.256
Join the study.

26
00:01:25.048 --> 00:01:29.640
On an iPhone, the app first asks you to add it to your Home Screen, because

27
00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:31.232
reminders only work there.

28
00:01:31.232 --> 00:01:33.987
Tap the Share button at the bottom of Safari,

29
00:01:34.371 --> 00:01:35.950
then, Add to Home Screen,

30
00:01:36.332 --> 00:01:37.143
and Add.

31
00:01:37.675 --> 00:01:43.268
Now open Home Comfort from its new icon, and always use this icon from now on.

32
00:01:43.268 --> 00:01:48.932
On Android, use the three dot menu in Chrome, and choose Add to Home screen, or

33
00:01:48.932 --> 00:01:49.792
Install app.

34
00:01:50.187 --> 00:01:50.439
Tap:

35
00:01:50.439 --> 00:01:51.258
I'm new here.

36
00:01:51.258 --> 00:01:55.414
Joining has eight short steps, and every question needs an answer.

37
00:01:55.805 --> 00:01:57.101
Step one is about you:

38
00:01:57.101 --> 00:01:59.988
your name and email, which you'll use to sign in.

39
00:01:59.988 --> 00:02:04.819
Then your gender, the year you were born, your height in feet and inches, and your

40
00:02:04.819 --> 00:02:05.821
weight in pounds.

41
00:02:05.821 --> 00:02:07.647
And which sounds most like you:

42
00:02:07.647 --> 00:02:12.125
you feel the cold easily, you're about average, or you feel the heat easily.

43
00:02:12.513 --> 00:02:16.417
If you miss something, the app shows you exactly what, right where it is.

44
00:02:16.813 --> 00:02:17.373
Step two:

45
00:02:17.373 --> 00:02:21.725
your ZIP code, used only to match your check-ins to the local weather.

46
00:02:21.725 --> 00:02:26.700
And whether you own your home, rent it, live in subsidized housing, or something

47
00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:27.010
else.

48
00:02:27.391 --> 00:02:28.079
Step three:

49
00:02:28.079 --> 00:02:29.204
your type of home.

50
00:02:29.589 --> 00:02:31.232
Detached stands on its own.

51
00:02:31.627 --> 00:02:35.104
Semi-attached shares one wall, like a twin or a duplex.

52
00:02:35.491 --> 00:02:37.859
Attached is a row house, or a townhouse.

53
00:02:38.246 --> 00:02:39.857
Or an apartment, or condo.

54
00:02:39.857 --> 00:02:42.769
The app then also asks which floor you live on.

55
00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:44.504
Step four:

56
00:02:44.504 --> 00:02:48.927
slide to your floor area in square feet, counting every heated floor.

57
00:02:48.927 --> 00:02:51.362
A good guess is fine, or tap Not sure.

58
00:02:51.362 --> 00:02:55.528
Then choose when your home was built, and how many floors it has.

59
00:02:55.528 --> 00:02:58.412
Count the basement only if people live in it.

60
00:02:58.797 --> 00:02:59.392
Step five:

61
00:02:59.392 --> 00:03:04.329
with minus and plus, set your bedrooms, and the adults, children, and pets who live

62
00:03:04.329 --> 00:03:04.864
with you.

63
00:03:04.864 --> 00:03:09.860
Then tell us how many others sleep in your bedroom, and whether your bedroom has its

64
00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:12.834
own thermostat, or shares one with the whole home.

65
00:03:13.223 --> 00:03:13.764
Step six:

66
00:03:13.764 --> 00:03:15.207
how is your home heated?

67
00:03:15.207 --> 00:03:16.530
Choose all that apply.

68
00:03:16.917 --> 00:03:19.712
A forced air furnace blows warm air through vents.

69
00:03:20.101 --> 00:03:24.901
A heat pump is electric, with a unit outside, and often cools in summer, too.

70
00:03:25.285 --> 00:03:29.360
A ductless mini-split has slim units, high on the wall, in each room.

71
00:03:29.745 --> 00:03:32.753
A boiler heats water, or steam, for radiators.

72
00:03:33.138 --> 00:03:36.679
Electric baseboard heaters run along the bottom of the walls.

73
00:03:37.074 --> 00:03:39.378
A wood or pellet stove heats one room.

74
00:03:39.762 --> 00:03:43.069
Or choose something else, like space heaters, or no heating.

75
00:03:43.463 --> 00:03:45.025
Next, your thermostat:

76
00:03:45.025 --> 00:03:50.917
a manual dial you turn by hand, a programmable one that follows a schedule, a smart

77
00:03:50.917 --> 00:03:56.028
Wi-Fi one like a Nest or an Ecobee, one your landlord controls, or none.

78
00:03:56.028 --> 00:03:59.506
Then set your usual temperature, or tap Not sure.

79
00:03:59.893 --> 00:04:00.619
Step seven:

80
00:04:00.619 --> 00:04:01.146
windows.

81
00:04:01.146 --> 00:04:03.125
Look at the edge of the glass.

82
00:04:03.125 --> 00:04:07.873
One sheet is single pane, two with a gap is double, and three is triple.

83
00:04:07.873 --> 00:04:08.203
Then:

84
00:04:08.203 --> 00:04:09.984
can your windows be opened?

85
00:04:10.377 --> 00:04:11.750
Next, two directions.

86
00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:16.520
They matter a lot, because the sun warms each side of a home differently.

87
00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:18.415
Use your phone's compass app:

88
00:04:18.415 --> 00:04:21.618
on an iPhone, swipe down, and search for Compass.

89
00:04:21.618 --> 00:04:24.820
On Android, search for compass in the Google app.

90
00:04:25.214 --> 00:04:31.985
Hold the phone flat, point its top edge the way the question asks, and read the big

91
00:04:31.985 --> 00:04:33.454
number and letter.

92
00:04:33.454 --> 00:04:35.411
Here, 271° W means west.

93
00:04:35.802 --> 00:04:40.410
For your bedroom window, stand at the window with your back to the room, and point

94
00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:40.635
out.

95
00:04:40.635 --> 00:04:45.018
Tap the matching letters, or type the number, and the app picks the direction.

96
00:04:45.408 --> 00:04:49.852
For the side of your home, stand in the middle of your home, and point toward your

97
00:04:49.852 --> 00:04:50.286
bedroom.

98
00:04:50.286 --> 00:04:51.424
Here, it's northeast.

99
00:04:51.805 --> 00:04:52.579
Step eight:

100
00:04:52.579 --> 00:04:55.885
check everything, and tap Edit to fix anything.

101
00:04:55.885 --> 00:04:59.261
Then choose a four digit PIN, and type it again.

102
00:04:59.261 --> 00:05:03.130
With your email, it lets you sign in on another device.

103
00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:03.763
Then tap:

104
00:05:03.763 --> 00:05:04.818
Join the study.

105
00:05:07.586 --> 00:05:11.053
The study team checks every sign-up, usually within a day.

106
00:05:11.053 --> 00:05:14.221
Your participant code is at the bottom of the screen.

107
00:05:14.608 --> 00:05:18.149
Once you're approved, open the app, or tap Check again, and you're in!

108
00:05:18.541 --> 00:05:20.365
Now, turn on notifications.

109
00:05:20.365 --> 00:05:25.297
The study needs them, to remind you about once an hour while you're home.

110
00:05:25.297 --> 00:05:25.567
Tap:

111
00:05:25.567 --> 00:05:27.053
Turn on notifications.

112
00:05:27.434 --> 00:05:28.501
Then tap Allow.

113
00:05:28.893 --> 00:05:33.424
Reminders come every day, from seven in the morning to ten at night.

114
00:05:33.424 --> 00:05:35.889
Tap the reminders box to change that.

115
00:05:35.889 --> 00:05:41.086
You can set different hours for weekdays and weekends, or add a second period.

116
00:05:41.086 --> 00:05:42.418
Then tap Save hours.

117
00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:44.898
Your Today screen shows your goals:

118
00:05:44.898 --> 00:05:47.822
four check-ins a day, and seven goal days a week.

119
00:05:47.822 --> 00:05:49.850
A day counts once it reaches four.

120
00:05:50.232 --> 00:05:52.124
And that's just the basic goal!

121
00:05:52.124 --> 00:05:56.886
Reminders come every hour while you're home, and every extra check-in is truly

122
00:05:56.886 --> 00:05:57.618
appreciated.

123
00:05:57.618 --> 00:06:02.685
Each one you share helps us learn how New Yorkers really feel at home, so homes can

124
00:06:02.685 --> 00:06:06.836
be heated around people, not just around a number on the thermostat.

125
00:06:06.836 --> 00:06:10.925
Together, we can make New York homes more comfortable for everyone.

126
00:06:11.311 --> 00:06:13.676
Later, at home, a reminder appears.

127
00:06:13.676 --> 00:06:14.959
Tap it to check in.

128
00:06:15.347 --> 00:06:15.740
First:

129
00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:16.787
are you at home?

130
00:06:16.787 --> 00:06:18.881
Only check in while you're home.

131
00:06:18.881 --> 00:06:19.143
Tap:

132
00:06:19.143 --> 00:06:20.845
Yes, for over an hour, or:

133
00:06:20.845 --> 00:06:22.088
Yes, I just got in.

134
00:06:22.470 --> 00:06:23.334
Question one:

135
00:06:23.334 --> 00:06:25.060
how do you feel right now?

136
00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:30.307
Seven choices, from hot, through neutral, which means neither warm nor cool, to

137
00:06:30.307 --> 00:06:30.640
cold.

138
00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:32.433
Tap the one that fits best.

139
00:06:32.818 --> 00:06:33.648
Question two:

140
00:06:33.648 --> 00:06:34.988
what are you wearing?

141
00:06:34.988 --> 00:06:37.605
Tap everything you have on, blankets too.

142
00:06:37.605 --> 00:06:42.775
The figure dresses as you tap, and the number shows how warm your outfit is, in a

143
00:06:42.775 --> 00:06:43.796
unit called clo.

144
00:06:43.796 --> 00:06:48.263
From your second check-in, Same as last time fills it in with one tap.

145
00:06:48.779 --> 00:06:49.135
Three:

146
00:06:49.135 --> 00:06:52.043
what have you been doing for the last 15 minutes?

147
00:06:52.043 --> 00:06:55.840
Sleeping, sitting, desk work, cooking, walking around, and more.

148
00:06:56.223 --> 00:06:56.515
Four:

149
00:06:56.515 --> 00:06:57.797
which room are you in?

150
00:06:57.797 --> 00:07:02.228
Your bedroom, the living room, the kitchen, a home office, the bathroom, the

151
00:07:02.228 --> 00:07:03.860
basement, or somewhere else.

152
00:07:04.248 --> 00:07:05.160
Question five:

153
00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:08.156
can you feel air moving around you, right now?

154
00:07:08.156 --> 00:07:11.935
This isn't about the temperature, only about air movement.

155
00:07:11.935 --> 00:07:17.406
Think of a draft from a window or a door, warm air blowing from a heating vent, or a

156
00:07:17.406 --> 00:07:17.667
fan.

157
00:07:18.061 --> 00:07:18.466
Choose:

158
00:07:18.466 --> 00:07:22.221
No, the air feels still, if you can't feel any air moving at all.

159
00:07:22.606 --> 00:07:26.489
Yes, a little, if you can just feel a gentle flow of air on your skin.

160
00:07:26.882 --> 00:07:27.067
Or:

161
00:07:27.067 --> 00:07:30.573
Yes, clearly, if you can clearly feel air blowing on you.

162
00:07:30.961 --> 00:07:31.807
Question six:

163
00:07:31.807 --> 00:07:33.500
is the sun shining on you?

164
00:07:33.882 --> 00:07:34.283
Choose:

165
00:07:34.283 --> 00:07:39.032
Sun on me, if direct sunlight falls on you, or on where you're sitting, for example

166
00:07:39.032 --> 00:07:40.005
through a window.

167
00:07:40.388 --> 00:07:43.929
No direct sun, if it's daytime, but the sun isn't on you.

168
00:07:44.317 --> 00:07:44.500
Or:

169
00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:49.181
It's dark, if it's evening or night, or if the blinds or curtains are closed.

170
00:07:49.562 --> 00:07:49.936
Seven:

171
00:07:49.936 --> 00:07:52.370
what did you do in the last 30 minutes?

172
00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:55.676
Only things you actually did, not how things are now.

173
00:07:55.676 --> 00:07:58.484
If a window was already closed, don't choose:

174
00:07:58.484 --> 00:07:59.607
I closed a window.

175
00:07:59.607 --> 00:08:01.229
Choose all that apply, or:

176
00:08:01.229 --> 00:08:02.789
I didn't do any of these.

177
00:08:03.289 --> 00:08:03.674
Eight:

178
00:08:03.674 --> 00:08:08.807
in the last 30 minutes, did you have a hot or cold drink, eat something, or feel

179
00:08:08.807 --> 00:08:10.412
hungry, tired, or unwell?

180
00:08:10.412 --> 00:08:11.502
Or none of these.

181
00:08:11.894 --> 00:08:15.969
Check your answers, tap the pencil to change one, then tap Save check-in.

182
00:08:16.352 --> 00:08:16.690
Saved!

183
00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:19.051
For a few seconds, you can still tap Undo.

184
00:08:19.051 --> 00:08:22.987
You'll see your progress for today, and when your next check-in opens.

185
00:08:23.371 --> 00:08:26.073
Check-ins need at least an hour between them.

186
00:08:26.073 --> 00:08:31.117
Until then, Today shows when the next one opens, and if you tap early, the app tells

187
00:08:31.117 --> 00:08:32.438
you when to come back.

188
00:08:32.829 --> 00:08:34.512
Out when a reminder comes?

189
00:08:34.512 --> 00:08:36.065
Start the check-in, tap:

190
00:08:36.065 --> 00:08:38.913
No, I'm out, and choose when to check again.

191
00:08:38.913 --> 00:08:40.660
Reminders pause until then.

192
00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:42.343
Going away for a few days?

193
00:08:42.343 --> 00:08:44.349
Turn reminders off in Settings.

194
00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:47.045
My comfort shows your comfort story:

195
00:08:47.045 --> 00:08:51.253
how you feel, at what times of day, and your check-ins day by day.

196
00:08:51.253 --> 00:08:55.715
My home shows your home profile, and Settings has your reminder hours.

197
00:08:57.043 --> 00:08:57.736
That's it.

198
00:08:57.736 --> 00:09:00.854
Thank you for taking part in Home Comfort NY!

199
00:09:00.854 --> 00:09:01.824
Any questions?

200
00:09:01.824 --> 00:09:04.872
Email Alireza, at the address on the screen.

